cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Sage-GPT: A Sanskrit-Only Small Language Model Trained from Scratch"
message: "If you use this software in your research or systems, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Rawat"
    given-names: "Rajendra Singh"
    alias: "airawatraj"
    affiliation: "cogni.chat"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-5017-1341"
repository-code: "https://github.com/airawatraj/sage-gpt"
url: "https://github.com/airawatraj/sage-gpt"
abstract: >-
  Sage-GPT is a Sanskrit-only Small Language Model (SLM) with ~7.5M parameters,
  trained entirely from scratch on a specialised corpus of ~140M ultra-pure Sanskrit
  tokens. It is not a fine-tuned version of an existing LLM — it is built ground-up,
  specifically for classical and Vedic Sanskrit literature. The architecture is a
  decoder-only Transformer featuring SwiGLU activations, Rotary Positional Embeddings
  (RoPE), RMSNorm, weight-tied input/output embeddings, and a SentencePiece unigram
  tokenizer with an 8,192-word vocabulary tuned for Sanskrit sandhi and compound words.
keywords:
  - "Sanskrit"
  - "small language model"
  - "transformer"
  - "natural language processing"
  - "low-resource languages"
  - "classical languages"
  - "Vedic"
  - "SwiGLU"
  - "RoPE"
  - "SentencePiece"
